   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Migration Management in African States through Capacity Building on Integrated Border Management and Countering Irregular Migration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project proposes to intervene and support the understanding and growth of complex issues within the framework of an integrated border management approach. In addition, it will afford officers an opportunity to understand and intervene on the issue in both their regional and national contexts and also within the international arena to respond effectively to challenges. This project will further contribute to the increased knowledge, understanding and skills in handling matters directly related to migration management such as screening travelers, investigation of reported cases of human trafficking. Additionally, the process intends to build a repository of knowledge on migration management and border control topics including creating an environment of mentorship via the African Capacity Building Centre.</narrative>
  </description>
